##
# Test accounts for //kernel:sbsa_pam_session_test (docs/base/session.md,
# "PAM"), added to base/etc's master.passwd in //images:pam_session_root
# only; never in the system's own root. Both have the password "neodarwin".
# test's hash is SHA-512 crypt, the format passwd(1) writes ("$6$", a
# 16-character salt, 5000 rounds), made by //tests/crypt:crypt_hash:
#   crypt_hash neodarwin '$6$K2DnKGs2OI7SVsY5'
# guest's is traditional DES (salt "nd"), the format libc had before, kept
# to show that such hashes still log in.
# test is in group admin (tests/qemu/pam/BUILD.bazel), so su(1) lets it
# become root; guest isn't.
##
test:$6$K2DnKGs2OI7SVsY5$TWI4VPZYjNpKLP8DhaNm7pTdz6G7vHtXwRbQyjJPLTG6s7Mn3yQIfKTzfobAqRsF7SMUERPgdgJJEXdDJPuu50:501:20::0:0:PAM Test User:/Users/test:/bin/zsh
guest:ndic/XPiorxqM:502:20::0:0:PAM Test Guest:/Users/guest:/bin/zsh
